From 766aba815a4abb153a9ecfe3a521cd8d8084fe51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrik Eriksson <patrik.m.eriksson@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:30:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] rec, web, cdng: fixes from the review of the seven
 commits above

Why: the review of this series (kb working/dng-chain/V/PATCHES.md) found no logic bug but four
things to fix, and the verification of the hypotheses behind the series changed two of its
claims. Note on history: the commits "media: trim after a delete made outside Core, and after
every pre-roll clip delete" and "media: noatime and umask on the re-insert mount" carry each
other's hunks (the first holds the free-space trim and the mount options, the second the pre-roll
trim); the messages are right, the split is not. The branch is not rewritten here; a clean
eight-commit series exists in the kb's patch backup (working/dng-chain/patches/).

What: the old standalone "dropped_copy_slot=" stats line is removed (the field is on the main
line since the previous commit); APERTAR_WEB_PREVIEW_RECORDING_FPS rejects non-finite values and
treats values below 0.5 as 0 (the interval cast was undefined for NaN); rawTakeActive() sits after
frameBufferStatus(), under its own comment; the lossy DNG writer honours APERTAR_DNG_DONTNEED like
the cDNG writer (no sync thread there, so "sync" behaves as "off"); the web-preview comment cites
the kb's profile (about 0.2 to 0.5 ms per frame, V/H4) instead of calling the pass the first
candidate. The raw-pool change of this series is hygiene with an expected effect on drops near
zero (V/H5: libcamera's thread meets the held mutex only when the copy worker already lags by
most of a frame period).

Tested: tools/dng_payload_write_test.sh passes; CameraController.cpp syntax-checks with the
libcamera block on (no new errors); ApertarCoreApp.cpp and LossyDngEncoder.cpp syntax-check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1zNNwfkFFgzHEzb7wV
